        <body>
            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="CLE01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Muzio</forename>
                        <surname>Clementi</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1752-01-23">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1832-03-10"/>
                    <occupation>composer</occupation>
                    <occupation>pianist</occupation>
                    <occupation>music teacher</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>The mention of Clemonti (19.06.1813) looks to be a mis-spelling (it does look like an 'o' in the MS but Godwin's 'o's are quite similar
  to his 'e's): he is not at home and when Godwin calls with <persName key="CLA01">Mary Jane</persName> a couple of days later he spells the name correctly.</p>
                        <p>Identification is strengthened by the fact that the dates fit - Clementi disppears from the diary between 1801 and 1811 and the <title>DNB</title> states that he was 
  out of England travelling from 1802 -10. </p>
                        <p>Clementi's second wife, who he married in 1811, was Emma Gisborne, whose brother was <persName key="GIS01">John Gisborne</persName>, second husband of <persName key="REV01">Maria Reveley</persName>.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="MS"> MS. Abinger c. 7, fol. 72: 25 October 1801</bibl>
                    <bibl type="printedbook"><title>Shelley and his Circle, 1773-1822</title>, ed. by Kenneth Neill Cameron and 
    Donald H. Reiman, 10 vols (Cambridge, Mass.: Harvard University Press, 1961-2002), X.1120n.</bibl>
                    <bibl type="other">
                        <title>DNB</title>
                    </bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
